WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
^- Hi, Mom.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
^- Hi, Mom.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:03.574
(laughing)

00:00:03.574 --> 00:00:04.407
Brandon!

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:07.926
(playful music)

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.110
- Hi, I'm Michelle.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.943
- I'm Brandon.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.470
- Today, we're going to be making kimchi

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.040
for the very first time.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.800
- [Brandon] Kimchi is a traditional Korean side dish,

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.330
made from fermented vegetables and a bunch of spice.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.530
- It's like the foundation of Korean food.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.748
- It's a very pungent dish.

00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:23.920
- You can eat it with like any meal.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.070
- I never thought I really had the skills to make it.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.210
- Watching my mom do it,

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.110
it just looked like a lot of physical labor.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.220
- So this time my mom is the one teaching us

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.150
how to make kimchi.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.830
- I've actually met Brandon's mom.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.680
She's just the nicest person ever.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.770
- I'm super nervous.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.220
She'll probably embarrass me.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.383
- Brandon!

00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.216
Brandon!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.183
It's too big.

00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:42.257
^(speaking foreign language)

00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:43.090
(laughing)

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.913
- First time kimchi making, let's do it.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.033
- My name is, I am Brandon's mom.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.422
I'm very exciting today.

00:00:48.422 --> 00:00:52.089
^(speaking foreign language)

00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:55.910
- Brandon and Michelle, are you today ready?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:56.743
- Yeah, sure.

00:00:56.743 --> 00:00:57.810
- As ready as I'll ever be.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.300
- This morning we actually did the first step already.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.811
It was a lot of salt and water and soaking the cabbages in.

00:01:02.811 --> 00:01:04.160
^- [Producer] It was the first time you did it, right?

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.000
- I didn't do it, my mom did it.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.723
^I just watched, visual learner.

00:01:06.771 --> 00:01:08.433
^(speaking foreign language)

00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:09.266
(laughing)

00:01:09.266 --> 00:01:10.099
^- Thanks mom.

00:01:10.099 --> 00:01:13.060
^(speaking foreign language)

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.383
- Sweet rice flour.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.160
- [Michelle] I didn't realize we

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.798
had to use flour to make kimchi.

00:01:19.798 --> 00:01:23.465
^(speaking foreign language)

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.730
^(laughing)

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:31.771
- Fellas, I'm ready.

00:01:31.771 --> 00:01:35.438
^(speaking foreign language)

00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:42.280
- Try, Brandon.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.947
^(speaking foreign language)

00:01:49.199 --> 00:01:50.449
- Here your finger, here.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.033
- Okay, I got it.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.250
That's a bad knife.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.703
- No, very good.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:58.870
- [Michelle] Oh my God.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:01:59.723
- Brandon, power.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.563
Ooh, too big.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.633
Okay, stop.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.633
Michelle.

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:05.466
- It's harder than you think.

00:02:05.466 --> 00:02:07.763
- Is this how skinny is should be?

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.653
- Brandon.

00:02:08.763 --> 00:02:11.010
(laughing)

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.010
- Good job, Brandon.

00:02:15.294 --> 00:02:16.275
- Weren't you a food writer?

00:02:16.275 --> 00:02:17.108
- Shh.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.992
- Brandon, C.

00:02:18.992 --> 00:02:21.100
(laughing)

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.663
- Michelle, B.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.237
- Oh, I feel when you're a parent,

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.800
you get better cooking skills.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:28.984
Like kimchi pad-awon.

00:02:28.984 --> 00:02:29.817
- Yeah.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.500
(speaking foreign language)

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.230
- I think I'd be better at this.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.260
Oh no, nevermind.

00:02:35.475 --> 00:02:37.384
^(laughing)

00:02:37.384 --> 00:02:40.530
- There's nothing sweeter than the approval of a Korean mom.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.330
- I've been trying for the approval, 22 years.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.143
- This one is just option.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.335
- Michelle's bad too.

00:02:46.335 --> 00:02:47.934
^(speaking foreign language)

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.440
- She like scrapes with her knife off her palm.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.273
- I know.

00:02:50.273 --> 00:02:51.106
- I like it.

00:02:51.814 --> 00:02:55.481
^(speaking foreign language)

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.033
- Grinding it?

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:57.866
Grating not grinding.

00:02:57.866 --> 00:02:59.891
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:00.950
- I could do this.

00:03:01.956 --> 00:03:03.316
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.149
- [Michelle] I love ginger.

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:04.982
^- Can I do it?

00:03:04.982 --> 00:03:06.270
^(speaking foreign language)

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.310
- Brandon, you try.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.403
- Ooh, yeah, I'm good at this.

00:03:09.403 --> 00:03:10.363
Is it A?

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.893
- Yeah, A plus.

00:03:11.893 --> 00:03:14.790
- Now that we grated up all the onions, ginger, and pear,

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.753
^we just put it into our original base.

00:03:17.146 --> 00:03:21.207
^- Literally every Korean mom has one of these.

00:03:21.207 --> 00:03:23.020
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:23.853
- How much?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.460
- Hmm, I don't know.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.293
(laughing)

00:03:28.293 --> 00:03:31.563
- OG kimchi is when you just eye it, and you just know.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:33.843
- It's like mini salted shrimp.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.753
- Yeah.

00:03:34.753 --> 00:03:37.043
- It smells like the fish part of the market.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.200
- [Michelle] This looks way thicker

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.412
than I thought kimchi was.

00:03:41.412 --> 00:03:45.079
^(speaking foreign language)

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.430
- I would buy a squeeze bottle of this.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:50.753
- This is legit.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.730
You know because we have gloves on.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.580
- [Michelle] Yes.

00:03:57.558 --> 00:03:59.140
^(speaking foreign language)

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.483
- You have to rub it in while mixing it?

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:04.020
- Yeah.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.232
- It's like fun cause you get really hands on.

00:04:06.232 --> 00:04:08.634
^(speaking foreign language)

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:09.467
Thank you.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.102
- I feel like they've gotten closer.

00:04:11.102 --> 00:04:11.935
(laughing)

00:04:11.935 --> 00:04:13.403
And I feel really awkward being here.

00:04:13.403 --> 00:04:15.202
^- I think we're going to go shopping later without you.

00:04:15.202 --> 00:04:18.869
^(speaking foreign language)

00:04:22.505 --> 00:04:23.338
- Mm.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:24.843
- Good?

00:04:24.843 --> 00:04:25.676
- Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.691 --> 00:04:29.358
^(speaking foreign language)

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:30.850
- My mind is blown.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.350
I didn't know it was so deliberate.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.593
- I thought the cabbage gets thrown in,

00:04:33.593 --> 00:04:34.426
and you just mixed it around.

00:04:34.426 --> 00:04:35.259
^- Yeah!

00:04:35.431 --> 00:04:38.987
^Wow, honestly I did not know this is how it worked.

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.875
^(speaking foreign languague)

00:04:40.875 --> 00:04:42.125
- Inside, okay.

00:04:43.187 --> 00:04:45.684
^- This is our kimchi container, just to first to one.

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:48.533
^- Start from the back, take one layer.

00:04:50.369 --> 00:04:54.036
^(speaking foreign language)

00:04:55.877 --> 00:04:58.127
(laughing)

00:04:58.652 --> 00:05:00.070
- Alright, here we go.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.003
Throw it on there.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:01.933
- Brandon.

00:05:03.673 --> 00:05:07.340
^(speaking foreign language)

00:05:07.798 --> 00:05:08.860
- It'll be more tender now.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.250
Seeing how complicated this is, seeing how long it takes,

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.970
makes you appreciate all the mom's out there making kimchi.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:14.982
- Don't push it.

00:05:14.982 --> 00:05:15.815
- Okay (laughs).

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.481
- It's your baby, your kimchi baby.

00:05:17.481 --> 00:05:19.340
- [Brandon] Gotta be gentle, just a baby.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.173
^And there we go.

00:05:20.272 --> 00:05:22.470
^(speaking foreign language)

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.733
Last one.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.720
- [Michelle] Kimchi for days.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:29.127
Oh my God, I'm so excited, it's so beautiful.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.650
I could eat this whole thing.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.012
- This is traditional OG kimchi.

00:05:36.012 --> 00:05:38.262
(laughing)

00:05:39.774 --> 00:05:40.607
- This is really good.

00:05:40.607 --> 00:05:41.992
^- It's the love, you taste the love.

00:05:41.992 --> 00:05:43.600
^(speaking foreign language)

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.500
- I actually feel like I leveled up as a Korean.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.330
I'm definitely going to KaKaoTalk my mom,

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.670
tell her some cheesy thank you

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.033
^for doing this for so many years.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.170
^(speaking foreign language)

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:55.844
- To actually make it definitely really special.

00:05:55.844 --> 00:05:59.511
^(speaking foreign language)

00:05:59.574 --> 00:06:02.241
^(calming music)

00:06:06.473 --> 00:06:08.723
^(laughing)

00:06:09.073 --> 00:06:10.702
- She forgot an ingredient.

00:06:10.702 --> 00:06:12.476
- [Off Camera Woman] What is that?

00:06:12.476 --> 00:06:13.823
- [Brandon] Just garlic.

